# One line over the tokens: kind from the first bytes (w0), the length, the word state at the end; keywords
# by a perfect hash of the first twelve bytes. kc = kind, plus 256 if a newline after this token is a semicolon.
ev :s idx Te < idx Tem min 0 max @te N sel :e over - :len drop dup {text :w0 255 & :c0 @fam :f0 6 = w0 8 >> 255 & :c1 @fam 2 = & f0 2 = | :isnum drop e 1 - :e1 [text 105 = 7 e1 [ws :we 2 = we 6 = | 5 6 sel sel :knum drop w0 Neg 4 len 4 min - 8 * >> & :a s 4 + Tm min {text Neg 4 len 4 - 0 max 4 min - 8 * >> & :b s 8 + Tm min {text Neg 4 len 8 - 0 max 4 min - 8 * >> & :d drop drop drop a 237384805 * b 50017773 * + d 597714383 * + 12 >> 255 & :hk @kwa a = hk @kwb b = & hk @kwc d = & len 12 <= & hk @kwk * :kk 0 = 4 * kk + :kid drop c1 len 1 > * 9 * c0 1 * + len 61 * + 0 >> 255 & @opk :kop drop f0 1 = kid kop sel :x1 drop isnum knum x1 sel :x2 drop f0 4 = 8 x2 sel :x3 drop f0 3 = 9 x3 sel :x4 drop f0 5 = 0 x4 sel :kd @semitab 256 * kd + swap drop >kc
